shiki-go implements the native library and CLI functionality of Shiki 4.6.0.

This project includes Go translations of Shiki and vscode-textmate algorithms,
the upstream TextMate grammars and themes, the unmodified Oniguruma WebAssembly
binary, and HAST property metadata. It also reproduces behavior from Shiki's
transformers, colorized-brackets, stream, and CLI packages, hast-util-to-html,
property-information, stringify-entities, and ansis.

Shiki reference commit: 167a38fea19cfa92b760ba36e157589ca5801274
https://github.com/shikijs/shiki

Copyright and license notices for these components and their incorporated
grammars, themes, and regex engine are retained in the licenses directory.
The original authors retain their copyrights. The Go runtime dependencies
wazero and golang.org/x/sys are also covered by the notices in that directory.

Node.js packages under tools/reference are development dependencies only.
They are not invoked by the Go library or CLI.
